id: SCA-054
title: Missing pip requirements.txt without hash verification
category: supply-chain
severity: info
engine: absence
target:
  filenames: requirements.txt
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: --hash=sha256:
    message: No hash verification in requirements.txt — pip can install tampered or swapped packages. Dependency confusion attacks work because pip trusts version numbers, not content.
fix: Use pip install --require-hashes and pin all deps with --hash=sha256:<hash>. Generate with pip-compile --generate-hashes.
